@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Community Guidelines & Safety Pledge";
}

<div class="container py-4" style="max-width: 900px;">
    <div class="mb-4">
        <h1 style="font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Community Guidelines & Safety</h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">WhisperSpace was built for college students to share real struggles in a supportive, empathetic, and judgment-free environment.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="form-card mb-4">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">1. The Golden Rule of Empathy</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            Remember that behind every anonymous confession or thought is a real peer going through stress, doubt, or loneliness. Treat others with the same kindness and compassion you would hope to receive.
        </p>

        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">2. What Is Prohibited</h2>
        <ul style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Bullying & Harassment:</strong> Targeted attacks, shaming, or aggressive language against any individual or group.</li>
            <li><strong>Doxxing:</strong> Revealing student names, roll numbers, phone numbers, social media handles, or teacher identities.</li>
            <li><strong>Hate Speech:</strong> Disparaging comments based on gender, race, religion, sexual orientation, or regional background.</li>
            <li><strong>Academic Dishonesty & Cheating:</strong> Soliciting or posting leaked exam papers or paid assignment fraud.</li>
            <li><strong>Self-Harm Encouragement:</strong> Explicit discussions promoting self-harm or violence.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">3. Anonymity & Privacy</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            Posts and comments are completely decoupled from student accounts. You can generate random pseudonyms (e.g. <em>"Quiet Owl"</em>, <em>"Brave Seeker"</em>) anytime you submit a post.
        </p>

        <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1rem;">4. Post Reporting & Moderation</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0;">
            Any community member can flag a post or comment using the <strong>Report</strong> button. Reported items are immediately escalated to the student moderation dashboard for review and potential removal.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Student Support & Emergency Helpline Card -->
    <div class="form-card" style="border-left: 6px solid #e11d48; background: #fff5f5;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #9f1239; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Need Urgent Support?</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: #881337; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            If you or a student you know is going through a mental health crisis, feeling hopeless, or having thoughts of self-harm, please reach out to free, 24/7 confidential helplines:
        </p>
        <ul style="color: #881337; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
            <li><strong>Tele-MANAS (Govt of India):</strong> Call <strong>14416</strong> or <strong>1800-891-4416</strong> (24/7 Free)</li>
            <li><strong>Vandrevala Foundation:</strong> Call <strong>+91 9999 666 555</strong> (24/7 Free counseling)</li>
            <li><strong>KIRAN Mental Health Helpline:</strong> Call <strong>1800-599-0019</strong></li>
            <li><strong>College Counseling Cell:</strong> Visit your campus student welfare center or mentor.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
